  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Protocol design is the systems-engineering discipline of specifying the message formats, state transitions, and interaction rules that govern communication between independent components. It balances correctness, efficiency, extensibility, and security concerns before a formal specification is written. Protocol design decisions - such as framing, versioning, and error-handling strategy - directly shape the reliability and interoperability of the resulting system.",
